{"batchcomplete": true, "query": {"pages": [{"pageid": 78, "ns": 14, "title": "Category:Quote templates", "revisions": [{"revid": 78, "parentid": 0, "user": "FANDOM", "timestamp": "2022-01-19T16:52:17Z", "slots": {"main": {"contentmodel": "wikitext", "contentformat": "text/x-wiki", "content": "[[Category:Templates]]"}}}], "categories": [{"ns": 14, "title": "Category:Templates"}], "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2022-01-19T16:52:47Z", "lastrevid": 78, "length": 22, "new": true, "fullurl": "https://turtle-wow.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Quote_templates", "editurl": "https://turtle-wow.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Quote_templates?action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://turtle-wow.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Quote_templates"}, {"pageid": 140, "ns": 14, "title": "Category:Screenshots", "revisions": [{"revid": 140, "parentid": 0, "user": "FANDOM", "timestamp": "2022-01-19T16:52:17Z", "slots": {"main": {"contentmodel": "wikitext", "contentformat": "text/x-wiki", "content": "[[Category:Images]]"}}}], "categories": [{"ns": 14, "title": "Category:Images"}], "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2022-01-19T16:52:16Z", "lastrevid": 140, "length": 19, "new": true, "fullurl": "https://turtle-wow.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Screenshots", "editurl": "https://turtle-wow.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Screenshots?action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://turtle-wow.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Screenshots"}, {"pageid": 2048, "ns": 14, "title": "Category:Races", "revisions": [{"revid": 6135, "parentid": 6134, "user": "MPBunny91", "timestamp": "2024-10-29T00:38:30Z", "slots": {"main": {"contentmodel": "wikitext", "contentformat": "text/x-wiki", "content": "{{Race links}}\n\n'''Race''' is a term used in ''[[World of Warcraft]]'' to split various unique creatures into separate groups. Numerous races populate [[Azeroth]] including [[Elf|elves]], [[troll]]s, [[human]]s, [[orc]]s, [[gnome]]s, and [[murloc]]s, among many others. Many races can interbreed including humans, [[High elf|high elves]], [[Night elf|night elves]], [[ogre]]s, orcs, and [[draenei]] \u2014 producing offspring often called [[half-breed]]s.\n\nThe [[Warcraft universe|''Warcraft'' universe]] is inhabited by many sentient and sapient beings. These races speak many different [[language]]s, have different homelands and [[Racial Traits|racial traits]], and can pursue different [[class]]es. Though most races are native to the world of [[Azeroth]], some have arrived from other worlds, such as [[Draenor]]. The armies of the [[Burning Legion]] are notably culled from many conquered worlds throughout the [[Great Dark Beyond]].\n\n==Definition==\nBlizzard occasionally interchanges the terms species and race, giving them roughly the same meaning.<ref>[[The Warcraft Encyclopedia/High Elves and Blood Elves]]</ref> Though species is usually reserved for non-sapient creatures such as [[wolf|wolves]], or non-humanoid creatures like [[dragon]]s, the term is occasionally used to refer to races like elves, dwarves, humans, orcs, draenei, ogres, goblins, tauren, etc.<ref>[[The Dark Portal and the Fall of Stormwind]]</ref><ref>''[[Rise of the Horde]]'', pg. 251</ref> Such uses are rare, however, and entirely absent in newer material such as [[World of Warcraft: Chronicle]]."}}}], "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2025-12-19T14:24:18Z", "lastrevid": 6135, "length": 1581, "fullurl": "https://turtle-wow.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Races", "editurl": "https://turtle-wow.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Races?action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://turtle-wow.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Races"}, {"pageid": 2621, "ns": 14, "title": "Category:Scarlet Crusade", "revisions": [{"revid": 8060, "parentid": 0, "user": "Aeliren", "timestamp": "2025-04-17T05:26:56Z", "slots": {"main": {"contentmodel": "wikitext", 